### 2. amz_consolidator.py
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Version** | 1.0 |
| **Status** | ✅ Active |
| **Purpose** | Consolidates Amazon QOH (Quantity on Hand) files into Amazon_SOH.xlsx |
| **Location** | `...\SOH\Scripts\amz_consolidator.py` |
| **Launcher** | `run_amz.vbs` |
| **Input Format 1** | `Amazon QOH DDMMYY.xlsx` — 3-column simple format |
| **Input Format 2** | `Inventory_ASIN_Sourcing_Retail_Australia_Custom_DD-MM-YYYY_DD-MM-YYYY.xlsx` — VC dump |
| **Output** | `Amazon_SOH.xlsx` — one column per snapshot, latest in col B |
| **SOH Column** | `Sellable On Hand Units` |
| **Cleanup** | Deletes all matching Amazon and Inventory_ASIN files from Stage |
| **Dependencies** | pandas, openpyxl |
| **JSON State** | `amz_consolidator_state.json` |
| **Created** | 29-Jul-2026 |
| **Last Updated** | 29-Jul-2026 |

**Notes:**
- Auto-detects file format (simple 3-col vs VC dump)
- VC dump format: skips metadata header row, reads from row 1
- Handles duplicate ISBNs within a file — keeps highest SOH value
- Date extracted from filename for both formats

